    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a pretty intense way to put it. If it's basically just \"political archaeology\" as you say, then isn't the whole idea of judicial originalism just a facade? It feels like they aren't even trying to find the truth anymore, they're just making up a version of history that makes it impossible to pass any common-sense laws. Is there even a legitimate constitutional reason for this, or is it all just a way to protect certain interests?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
